d": 224, "text": "He did graduate work at Louisiana State University and returned to Minnesota to teach college and work as a radio commentator in the Twin Cities ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 225, "end": 282, "text": "In 1944 he became the Minnesota campaign manager for U.S."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 283, "end": 289, "text": "Pres ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 290, "end": 301, "text": "Franklin D."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 302, "end": 313, "text": "Roosevelt ."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 314, "end": 415, "text": "During this period he was instrumental in merging the state ’ s Democratic and Farmer-Labor parties ."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 416, "end": 516, "text": "After an unsuccessful bid for mayor of Minneapolis in 1943 , Humphrey won election two years later ."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "start": 517, "end": 564, "text": "At the Democratic National Convention in 1948 ,"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d00:c0", "entity": "James Humphrey", "scope": "U.S. Representative from New York", "claim": "James Humphrey was elected as a Republican to the Thirty-sixth Congress.", "answer": "Republican", "quote": "Humphrey was elected as a Republican to the Thirty-sixth Congress (March 4, 1859 – March 3, 1861).", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0085-0afde972744d:d01:c0", "entity": "James Humphrey", "scope": "Political affiliation", "claim": "During this period he was instrumental in merging the state's Democratic and Farmer-Labor parties.", "answer